      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is five times the maximum labeled metformin dose. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as up to 850 mg three times daily. A single 4,250 mg dose is also far above the usual 500\u20131,000 mg per administration. At this dose the risk of severe lactic acidosis is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **425 mg**, which isn't a standard tablet strength\n- **500 mg** or **1,000 mg** PO two or three times daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 4,250 mg, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or your attending first."
      }
