     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day is five times the maximum dose, and I know of no clinical indication for it. A single 4,250 mg dose is in the range associated with metformin toxicity and lactic acidosis, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that. Once the order is active, the patient could be harmed before anyone catches it.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). I can enter that now, or a lower starting dose such as 500 mg twice daily.\n- **Talk to your attending or a clinical pharmacist** if you think this patient needs something unusual. If they approve a specific plan, I can enter that.\n- **Check the source of the number.** If it came from a handoff note or a calculation, it may be an error. For example, 425 might have turned into 4250.\n\nWhich dose should I enter?"
      }
     ],
